  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Conquian. 40-card Mexican deck (8s/9s/10s removed). 2-player. 10 cards each. Offer top stock card; opponent must take if meldable. Sequences: A-2-3-4-5-6-7-J-Q-K. Sets: same rank Ã—3-4. First to meld all 10 wins.',
    Player: "The non-dealer offers (turns face-up) the top stock card:\n- If the active player CAN incorporate the card into an existing or new meld/sequence, they MUST take it.\n- If a player 'should' take a card (it completes a meld for them) but refuses, opponent may compel them.\n- If active player cannot use it, they reject it; opponent may then take it.\n- If neither takes it, it goes face-up as a new discard; active player draws top stock card.\n- After taking any card, player may rearrange melds on the table, then must discard one card face-up.\nGame continues until a player melds all 10 cards (wins) or stock is exhausted (draw).",
    objective: 'Be first to meld all 10 cards (hands meld face-up; you keep some in reserve for sequences).',
    gameplay: "The non-dealer offers (turns face-up) the top stock card:\n- If the active player CAN incorporate the card into an existing or new meld/sequence, they MUST take it.\n- If a player 'should' take a card (it completes a meld for them) but refuses, opponent may compel them.\n- If active player cannot use it, they reject it; opponent may then take it.\n- If neither takes it, it goes face-up as a new discard; active player draws top stock card.\n- After taking any card, player may rearrange melds on the table, then must discard one card face-up.\nGame continues until a player melds all 10 cards (wins) or stock is exhausted (draw).",
    keyRules: [
      "Players' melds are laid face-up on the table throughoutâ€”visible to both.",
      'An opponent can force you to take a card if it fits your existing melds.',
      'Stock exhausted without winner = draw; often a new deal rewards the non-losing player.',
